Phase 1 catalog experiment
==========================

LOAD 'test_doltgres' installs an opt-in relation-name projection hook. A name
"current_database/branch".schema.table (or @ alias) resolves to the real schema
"dg_<branch-byte-length>_<branch>_<schema>" and its real relation OID. Fixture
schemas must be created explicitly. Ordinary permissions, locks, snapshots,
relcache invalidation and prepared-plan dependencies apply to those objects.

This is not a complete branch implementation. No default session branch,
branch-qualified type/function lookup, CREATE namespace resolution, history,
canonical catalog serialization, prolly table AM, or version-control commit
exists here. Use aliases for branch-qualified FROM items. Branch names with
additional / or @ and projected names >= NAMEDATALEN fail explicitly. Physical
namespaces are only fixtures; their names are not a final mapping ABI.

Run in an assertion-enabled configured tree:
  make -C src/test/modules/test_doltgres check
or against a disposable installed server:
  make -C src/test/modules/test_doltgres installcheck

TAP tests start their own server and test cross-session cache invalidation,
branch lock separation, consistent snapshots, savepoints, and crash recovery of
prepared changes using PostgreSQL's existing heap WAL. They do NOT test custom
prolly WAL. The ordinary server is unchanged when the hook is NULL.
